 "result": "All of this is in `src/tessel/views.py` unless noted.\n\n**Building the view function**\n- `VerbView` subclasses `View` (`:138`). Its `__init_subclass__` (`:165`) scans for attributes named after the HTTP methods in `http_method_funcs` (`get`, `post`, …). It sets `cls.methods` to the upper-cased set, merged with any base-class `methods`.\n- `View.to_view_func(name, ...)` (`:86`) is a classmethod that returns a plain function `view(**kwargs)`.\n  - On each request, `view` instantiates the class (or reuses one instance when `init_every_request` is `False`) and calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`.\n  - It applies any `cls.decorators`.\n  - It copies `view_class`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` onto the function (`:129-134`).\n\n**Registering the route**\n- `App.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`) reads `view_func.methods` (`:623`, defaulting to `(\"GET\",)`) and `provide_automatic_options` (`:635`). It uses them to build the URL rule, so Werkzeug only matches the allowed methods.\n\n**Dispatch per request**\n- `VerbView.run_view` (`:182`) does `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`. `HEAD` falls back to `get` if there is no `head` handler. It then calls that handler through `ensure_sync` with the URL kwargs.",
